# Phase 3 execution log — continuation 2026-09-26T054243Z

## Goal and scope

- Continued Java 5.5.1 remoting behavior comparison; did not alter the Phase 3 plan. Phase 4 remains blocked.
- Reviewed Java GO_AWAY callback/retry flow and Rust async semaphore permit ownership.

## Source finding and implementation

- Java completes the first response future for GO_AWAY before retrying through `invokeImpl`, which releases the initial async semaphore permit; the retry then performs admission again.
- Rust retained the original `OwnedSemaphorePermit` across the retry and marked retry as already admitted. Changed invoke ownership to retain the permit in the outer invocation scope, explicitly drop it after GO_AWAY, and re-acquire admission under the same absolute deadline. Retry still skips outbound hooks.
- Added `p3_go_away_retry_reacquires_async_admission`: with async capacity 1, a competing invocation queued before GO_AWAY is allowed to acquire the released permit and complete before the retry can send. This makes the source-observed order testable.
- Updated `docs/compatibility/PHASE_3_REMOTING_INVENTORY.md` and `docs/compatibility/JAVA_5_5_1_COMPATIBILITY.md` with the behavior and test mapping.

